The Hoplite Titan is like the centaur of Greek mythology, except it has a lion's body instead of that of a horse. Ancient Greek hoplite soldiers used swords, shields, and spears to defeat their enemies. Like this Titan, Greek hoplites grouped together in battle so that their shields could overlap and thus create a stronger defense. Around the same era, an army of Hoplite Titans had been used by [[Jason]], who led the Argonauts. Allegedly, he was able to summon this army with his [[dragon's teeth]].

In modern times, [[Jason's logbook]] was used to locate the sunken ship, the [[Argo]], off the coast of [[Sutos Island]]. There, [[Zhalia Moon]] uncovered several Hoplite [[Amulets]] protected by a magical puzzle. Upon returning to find [[Lok Lambert]] and [[Sophie Casterwill]] fighting against a coalition of [[Suits]] and Sutos citizens, Zhalia gave both of her teammates a Hoplite Amulet so that they could stand their ground, and later on the team used these Titans for their easy summoning and for their great teamwork powers. {{source|Like Father, Unlike Son}}

Lok later invoked his Hoplite in [[Klaus' bookshop]] to fight [[Klaus]], that invoked [[Nighlurker]]. The two Titans fought until [[Dante Vale|Dante]], and later Sophie, invoked their own Hoplite Titans to help defeat Nighlurker, taking advantage of Hoplite's Teamwork ability. {{source|The Bookshop Hunter}}

Lok, while fighting for [[Cavalier]]'s [[Amulets|Amulet]] on his own, again used his Hoplite in the [[Mausoleum of Sir Lancelot]] in response to [[Rassimov]]'s [[Thornment]]. Hoplite was quickly made imobile by Thornment and sent back to its amulet. {{source|Memory Lane}}

Both Lok Lambert and Sophie Casterwill summoned, in addition to many other Titans, their Hoplite Titans to fight agaisnt [[Simon Judeau|the Professor]] and the three Legendary Titans in [[The Professor's castle|The Professor's Castle]]. The two Hoplite fought [[Behemoth]] along with [[Freelancer]] but were quickly overpowered by the much stronger Legendary Titan, and got sent back to their amulets. In the same episode, [[Zhalia Moon]] used her Hoplite alongside [[Gareon]] to fight the two [[Undergolem]] Titans summoned by [[Eathon the dog]] to guard the castle; Zhalia's Titans were eventually sent back to their amulets. {{source|The Mission}}

One Hoplite Titan, along with a Freelancer and an [[Ironsquire]] Titan, were somehow summoned by the [[Ring of Arc]] from nearby amulets at the [[Cathedral of Notre Dame]]. The three rogue Titans attacked [[Clements]]. [[Metz]], who was on a call with him at the time of the incident, is worried about the sudden lack of response from Clements, and calls the Huntik Team to investigate the issue. Upon arrival, Lok tried to handle Hoplite on his own with the use of the [[Willblade]], but was unsuccessful; Lok then summons [[Baselaird]] to fight Freelancer and Hoplite. Lok's Titan is succeseful in defeating Freelancer, and so [[Cherit]] delivers the final blow on Hoplite, sending it back to its amulet. {{source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}}
